{
  "id": "T18_32_explicit_baseline_begin_and_end_acts_are_validated_against_the_derivation",
  "family": "T18",
  "rules": [
    "10.2.9",
    "7.6.4",
    "7.6.5",
    "7.6.6",
    "8.1.2",
    "10.2.4",
    "I-17",
    "12.19"
  ],
  "description": "An identical write of a generated begin or end act is a replay: replayed, with nothing generated or recorded. Any other explicit baseline act fails 10.2.9: one that restates a transition another act already gives; one whose content differs from the derivation (an alignment that did not occur, a second ending of one begin act); one with a cause its unit does not allow; one whose target is not of the kind its action requires; one that has two targets; and a definite end content without policy. @period on a statement is a misplaced reserved member (10.2.4). Rejected writes leave nothing behind.",
